From e3334630daf3cdcd5237aece1ad84999aee44387 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:49:31 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): remote owner pass on its own watcher; expired
 notices scan the transcript once

The MacBook gateway admitted busy-chat remote notices 13-88 s after first sight and woke local chain
cards 25-60 s late against a 5 s notifier interval (t_01a1d4de28a8510d). Measured in-process
(hermes gateway profile): each remote owner pass spent 12-20 s in krn.collect asking transcript_has
for every card past LATE_MAX_S, before _claim_notice looked at the ledger. Two chats carried 158 and
207 such cards, all already settled, so the scans' answers were never used (365 scans = 12.15 s
uncontended). The pass ran inline in the notifier loop, so its cost became local wake latency.

- collect: the expired settle reason (transcript vs expired) is an _ExpiredReason that _claim_notice
  resolves only on the first settle (no ledger row); settled rows cost no scan.
- _kanban_remote_owner_watcher: supervised in _PRE_RECONNECT_WATCHERS, own INTERVAL_S cadence, the
  only caller of kanban_remote_owner.tick, honours kanban.notify_in_gateway, stops between passes.
- tick logs collect vs admit seconds when a pass exceeds 5 s.
